{
  "key": "letter-010-part-01",
  "number": 10,
  "generationId": "01a1e4e8-90de-7a4d-b396-98963858de9a",
  "voice": "Views",
  "speed": 0.9,
  "clips": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "My respects to you.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/01.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.2641269999999998
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "I was waiting for your letter when it came.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/02.mp3",
      "start": 2.8421089999999998,
      "end": 5.101791
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "I really want your life to be filled with light, for you to surrender yourself to God God and light are always close by.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/03.mp3",
      "start": 6.565465,
      "end": 13.893424
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "It is only a matter of opening one's eyes and then what is ours becomes ours.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/04.mp3",
      "start": 15.419388000000001,
      "end": 20.567392
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "The distance is just that of between the eyelash and the eye - and perhaps not even that much; the eyes are always open, only we don't know it.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/05.mp3",
      "start": 22.060159,
      "end": 30.658503
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "There is an old story: A fish had long heard stories about the ocean.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/06.mp3",
      "start": 32.240317000000005,
      "end": 37.206213
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "She began to fret about it so one day she asked the Queen of Fishes: What is this ocean and where is it?",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/07.mp3",
      "start": 38.637868000000005,
      "end": 45.422472
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "The Queen was surprised.",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/08.mp3",
      "start": 46.954036,
      "end": 48.434965999999996
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "She said: The ocean?",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/09.mp3",
      "start": 49.994331,
      "end": 52.811223999999996
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "Why, you are in the ocean itself!",
      "path": "audio/1963-10/10.mp3",
      "start": 54.302812,
      "end": 57.1
    }
  ]
}
